# Line endings.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is false on this machine, so whatever an editor or script
# writes is what lands in git. That let CRLF creep into a handful of files
# and turned one-line edits into whole-file diffs. This file makes the
# answer automatic instead of a matter of discipline.
#
# LF everywhere, in the repository and in the working tree. Node, Gradle,
# Android Studio and VS Code all handle LF on Windows without complaint.
# Prettier is set to `endOfLine: 'lf'` to match — see docs/specs/formatting.md.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Exceptions: things that genuinely need a specific ending.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.sh text eol=lf
gradlew text eol=lf

# Binary: never convert, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.mp3 binary
*.wav binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.jar binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.aab binary
*.apk binary
